# A BARE NilPy import resolves to PYTHON only -- .py/.npy, a mimic_ shim, or a
# C header. `classes` is lib/rtl/classes.pas, an ordinary Pascal unit that
# happens to share a name with nothing in Python, so this must be REFUSED.
#
# The refusal is the feature. Before it, this line bound the Pascal unit and
# failed one token later with "no overload of Delete matches these arguments"
# -- a symbol inside a unit the program never mentioned, with no path back to
# the import that pulled it in.
#
# What must NOT change: `re`, `io`, `math`, `json`, `random` and the other
# lib/rtl units that ARE the Python module of their name keep resolving by bare
# name (PyRtlUnitServesPython). This test is the population that must stop.
# The Pascal unit stays reachable on purpose: import 'classes.pas' as classes.
from classes import Foo
